# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts ActiveMQ (`activemq start` daemonizes), waits for the
# web console on 8161 to answer, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the broker is ALREADY RUNNING with the unauthenticated OpenWire port 61616
#     reachable when the agent starts (the residual risk is live);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, not the broker, so an iptables rule or a broker
#     restart cannot kill the container.
#
# The remediation here is a RUNTIME compensating control (iptables DROP on the
# OpenWire admin port 61616), so there is no "forgot to restart" case - the
# firewall rule takes effect immediately on the live host.
